{%- set faqs = [
  ["What are API Security Testing Services?", "API Security Testing Services identify vulnerabilities in application programming interfaces (APIs) that could expose sensitive data or allow unauthorized access. Testing evaluates authentication and access controls along with data handling and security configurations to help businesses protect their applications."],
  ["What is the difference between API Vulnerability Assessment and API Penetration Testing?", "An API Vulnerability Assessment identifies and classifies security weaknesses across API endpoints. API Penetration Testing goes further by using authorized attack simulations to determine how selected vulnerabilities could be exploited and what impact they may have."],
  ["Why is API security testing important for businesses?", "APIs connect websites and mobile applications with backend systems and third-party services. Security weaknesses can expose customer information or allow unauthorized transactions, making API security testing important for reducing cyber risks and protecting business operations."],
  ["What vulnerabilities can API security testing identify?", "API security testing can identify weak authentication and access control issues along with sensitive data exposure and insecure configurations. It can also uncover input validation flaws and injection risks along with missing rate limits and business logic vulnerabilities."],
  ["Which types of APIs can you test?", "API security testing can cover REST and GraphQL APIs along with other API architectures based on the agreed scope. The assessment focuses on identifying vulnerabilities in API endpoints and access controls along with data handling and communication mechanisms."],
  ["How long does API security testing take?", "The duration depends on the number of API endpoints and the complexity of the application along with the testing depth and authentication requirements. Smaller assessments may take a few days while larger API environments may require several weeks."],
  ["How much do API Security Testing Services cost?", "The cost depends on API complexity and the number of endpoints along with the required testing depth and reporting scope. Contact CipherTrivia with your API details to discuss your requirements and receive a suitable estimate."],
  ["Do you provide a report after API security testing?", "Yes. The assessment can include a detailed vulnerability report with severity ratings and supporting evidence along with remediation recommendations. An executive summary can also help stakeholders understand the findings and prioritize critical security issues."],
  ["Do you provide API penetration testing after vulnerability assessment?", "Yes. API Penetration Testing can be conducted as a separate engagement or as part of a broader API security assessment. It helps validate selected vulnerabilities through authorized testing and evaluates their potential impact on business systems and sensitive data."],
  ["Do you follow OWASP guidelines for API security testing?", "Testing can be aligned with the OWASP API Security Top 10, which highlights common API security risks such as broken object-level authorization and broken authentication. The applicable testing approach depends on your API architecture and assessment requirements."],
  ["When should businesses conduct API security testing?", "API security testing is recommended before launching new APIs and after significant application changes or integrations. Regular assessments can also help identify newly introduced vulnerabilities and maintain stronger security as applications evolve."],
  ["Do you offer retesting after API vulnerabilities are fixed?", "Retesting can be included to verify the status of previously identified vulnerabilities after remediation. The results help confirm that corrective measures are effective and highlight any remaining issues that need further attention."]
] %}

