<!-- PROCESS                                                              -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->
<section class="section section--ink" aria-labelledby="s5-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="process">
      <div class="process__aside">
        <h2 class="process__title" id="s5-title">Our API Security Testing Process</h2>
        <p class="process__lede">CipherTrivia follows a structured API Security Testing process to identify vulnerabilities and help businesses protect their APIs from unauthorized access and data exposure. Our approach combines API Vulnerability Assessment with API Penetration Testing to uncover security gaps and provide practical recommendations for improving API protection.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="process__list" data-process>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Scope Definition and API Discovery</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We begin by understanding your application architecture and business requirements to identify the APIs included in the assessment. This helps define the testing scope and prioritize critical endpoints that handle sensitive data or business operations.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">API Vulnerability Assessment</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Our team examines API endpoints and security settings to identify weaknesses in authentication and access controls along with data handling and input validation. This stage helps uncover common vulnerabilities that could expose business information or affect application security.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">API Penetration Testing</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Through authorized testing, we investigate identified weaknesses to determine how they could be exploited in real-world attack scenarios. Our API Penetration Testing Services focus on risks such as unauthorized data access and insecure API requests along with flaws in important business functions.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Risk Analysis and Prioritization</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Each identified vulnerability is assessed based on its severity and potential impact on your business. Findings are prioritized to help your development team focus on critical issues and plan remediation efficiently.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Security Reporting and Recommendations</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We deliver a detailed report covering identified vulnerabilities and their potential impact along with recommended corrective actions. The report helps technical teams understand each issue and take appropriate steps to address API security weaknesses.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Remediation Verification and Retesting</h3>
          <p class="step__text">After fixes are implemented, retesting can be conducted to verify that reported vulnerabilities have been addressed. This final stage helps confirm the effectiveness of corrective measures and highlights any remaining security concerns.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

